extend_sim examples
===================

extend_sim appends N copies of a reference sample (a LAMMPS data file)
onto the high end of the box along one axis.  See doc/extend_sim for the
full description.  All three scripts build their own sample.data with
lattice / create_atoms + write_data, so no external files are needed.
Requires the EXTRA-COMMAND package (and SHOCK for in.extend_sim.shock).

  in.prototype              pure input-script version of the algorithm,
                            kept as a reference (no extend_sim command)

  in.extend_sim.append      operate on the already-loaded system; a
                            periodic +z face is grown with change_box
                            and 3 sample copies are stacked -> 4x atoms

  in.extend_sim.restart     use the 'restart' keyword: build base.restart,
                            clear, then rebuild it extended by 2 slabs

  in.extend_sim.shock       wall/piston shock into a shrink-wrapped slab;
                            one slab appended after each batch of steps so
                            the box stays ahead of the wave (no change_box)

Run, e.g.:

  lmp -in in.extend_sim.append
  mpirun -np 4 lmp -in in.extend_sim.shock
